## Test it

```bat
"%PYTHON%" -m pytest mcp-servers/{{ name }}
```

The tests use local {{ "API responses from `" ~ responses_file ~ "`, keyed by method and path" if rest else "CSV data" }}.
They apply the workspace's policy rules to check what each role may see:

| Role | Tool call | Data |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `manager` | allowed | every column |
{% if plan.masked %}
| `analyst` | allowed | {% for column in plan.masked %}`{{ column }}`{{ ", " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %} {{ "is" if plan.masked | length == 1 else "are" }} masked, at most {{ analyst_rows }} rows |
{% else %}
| `analyst` | allowed | every column, at most {{ analyst_rows }} rows |
{% endif %}
| anything else | denied | none |

**Expected result:** the tests pass for allowed and denied callers. To change
behavior, add a test in `tests/test_{{ package }}.py` that sets the caller's roles,
calls the tool, and asserts the expected result.
{% if not sample %}
The generated tests check the columns each role sees. Add assertions for the
rows your application expects.
